WEBVTT

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:02.370
Your Highness!

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:03.980
You can do it!

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.570
Beat that hick!

00:00:08.390 --> 00:00:09.770
How sad.

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:12.990
They still expect the prince to win after 
the miserable fights they've witnessed.

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:16.520
Champions, begin!

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:24.410
<b>Trapped in</b>

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:26.750
<b>a Dating Sim</b>

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:31.380
<b>Trapped in
a Dating Sim</b>

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:52.440
It's Awesome

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:52.260
His Armor is the strongest 
currently available, huh?

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:55.220
While his Armor certainly appears 
to be better than the others,

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:56.910
that's really all it is.

00:01:56.910 --> 00:01:58.740
Then I just need to attack.

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:07.720
You can do it, Your Highness!

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:08.620
Beat him!

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:09.480
Please!

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:13.390
Looks like these guys really 
don't want to lose their bets.

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:16.360
I'm sure they'd be relieved to see you lose.

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:20.310
Perhaps they simply find your words 
and actions annoying as hell.

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:22.620
Don't use language like that!

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:24.730
Whoops.

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:27.750
I cannot lose!

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:31.250
For Marie's sake, I cannot lose!

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:34.380
I'll admit it at least has artistic value.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:36.010
You're being awfully complimentary.

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:40.860
Your Highness, you've got considerably 
more spirit than the other four.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:43.710
Perhaps they didn't try 
their hardest after all.

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:48.520
If you lose, then the other four can 
get closer to Marie without you.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:52.310
Nonsense. You know nothing about us.

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:56.900
That's right, I don't. But I don't think 
things should continue as they are.

00:02:57.330 --> 00:03:01.930
Your Highness, how does it 
feel to truly love someone?

00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:04.660
I don't really understand that sort of thing.

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:08.180
I'm sure you don't. It's the reason 
you're able to get in others' way.

00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:12.170
If you truly love someone, 
you should gracefully step aside for them.

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:15.840
Are you talking about Ms. Angelica?

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:19.670
I think she really loves you.

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:23.550
No! She didn't understand how I feel.

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:26.370
She's like the other women 
at the royal palace.

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:28.960
Nobody sees the real me.

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:31.810
I didn't want to be born into royalty.

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:35.130
Marie is the only one who noticed how I felt.

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:38.150
Marie is the only one who loved me!

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:43.530
In other words, you've been tricked by 
a type of woman not found at the palace.

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:44.790
Pathetic.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:45.780
Silence!

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:47.960
How dare you behave so haughtily?

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:51.790
You're only this arrogant because 
you've acquired such a powerful Armor!

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:57.060
Are you enjoying yourself?

00:03:57.060 --> 00:04:00.300
How does it feel to look down 
on someone and lecture them?

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:04.800
It's awesome.

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:08.850
I feel absolutely amazing.

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:14.570
It's true that I'm arrogant, 
but you guys still can't beat me.

00:04:14.570 --> 00:04:19.790
How does it feel to lose to someone 
you saw as beneath you, Prince?

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:22.090
Y-You bastard!

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:25.820
You didn't want to be born 
into royalty? Screw off.

00:04:26.170 --> 00:04:30.950
Have you ever been sold off by 
a pervy old hag and nearly died?

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:31.950
What?

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:38.190
Have you ever bowed your head to girls,
only to have them ruin your tea party?

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:43.700
We've been pushed aside 
just for <i>talking</i> to girls!

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:47.590
Do you have any idea how that feels?!

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:50.100
What are you boys crying about?

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:52.220
I won't lose.

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:55.350
I won't stop fighting until one of us is dead!

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:59.930
I'd rather die than have Marie taken from me!

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:06.790
The prince is serious about her.

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:11.150
He really does love that girl.

00:05:12.230 --> 00:05:14.000
Y-You're wrong!

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:17.750
Olivia?

00:05:18.730 --> 00:05:22.390
Perhaps the prince really does love Ms. Marie,

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:25.620
but... but...

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:29.860
Ms. Angelica loves the prince, too!

00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:33.770
She's been watching this battle in such pain.

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:38.050
No matter how much it hurts 
or how sad it makes her,

00:05:38.410 --> 00:05:41.270
she's kept her eyes on the prince.

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:45.720
Don't tell me that's not love!

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:53.820
Wow. She's not even using 
a loudspeaker or magic.

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:56.540
Yes. It's a mysterious power.

00:05:56.800 --> 00:05:58.700
<i>What's her deal?</i>

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:01.470
<i>You may have won over a mob 
character who's kinda strong,</i>

00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:05.050
<i>but there's still no place for 
you in this world anymore.</i>

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:07.050
You're saying Angelica...

00:06:07.530 --> 00:06:12.050
The feelings of a woman who sees 
me only as the prince are love?

00:06:12.550 --> 00:06:17.430
I found a woman who sees me 
for myself and understands me.

00:06:18.030 --> 00:06:19.730
That's true love.

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:23.940
Angelica, your feelings aren't love.

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:25.440
They're an imposition.

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:28.830
If you understand that, 
then never approach me again.

00:06:32.390 --> 00:06:33.700
Let us continue.

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:36.830
This duel won't end until one of us dies.

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:41.380
I admire your willingness to 
use your own life as a shield.

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:44.710
Not even I can kill a prince.

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:49.220
Good for you. You're going to 
win because you're the prince.

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:52.260
Despite claiming you wish 
you weren't born a prince,

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:55.180
you're making great use of your status.

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:57.100
It's praiseworthy.

00:06:57.100 --> 00:07:00.150
Go on, ask me to lose.

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:04.630
Ask me to lose because you don't 
want to leave your precious Marie.

00:07:04.630 --> 00:07:07.110
Why don't you order me to lose as the prince?

00:07:07.410 --> 00:07:11.990
I-I can't do that! This is a sacred duel!

00:07:12.310 --> 00:07:16.130
What? Are you telling me to 
pretend to lose on purpose?

00:07:16.130 --> 00:07:19.000
That would be too obvious.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:25.750
After all, there's no way you could pull 
off a comeback under these circumstances.

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:30.260
Th-This guy is awful...

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:32.530
Your Highness, don't let him beat you!

00:07:32.530 --> 00:07:33.790
Drop dead, shithead!

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:35.260
Die!

00:07:35.560 --> 00:07:38.790
Do you feel amazing right now?

00:07:38.790 --> 00:07:41.510
He'd never acknowledge it if I didn't say it.

00:07:41.510 --> 00:07:43.770
He'll rule a country in the future.

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:46.270
He can't allow someone 
like Marie to fool him.

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:48.810
So you played the villain?

00:07:48.810 --> 00:07:50.780
You seemed to enjoy yourself quite a bit.

00:07:51.040 --> 00:07:53.410
Yeah, it was super fun.

00:07:54.060 --> 00:07:56.910
Bartfort!

00:07:58.550 --> 00:08:01.150
Your Highness, shall we have 
a serious conversation?

00:08:01.150 --> 00:08:02.830
Let go, you fiend!

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:08.960
Antagonizing Ms. Angelica and the Redgrave 
family will threaten your noble status.

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:11.340
You could be stripped of 
your right to the throne.

00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:15.840
Will you really choose Marie regardless?

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:20.480
If you understand, then 
go to Ms. Angelica and—

00:08:20.480 --> 00:08:21.350
I don't need it.

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:22.850
What?

00:08:23.210 --> 00:08:25.940
I don't need my status or my honor.

00:08:26.910 --> 00:08:30.290
All I need is Marie.

00:08:32.330 --> 00:08:33.410
Luxion.

00:08:35.310 --> 00:08:39.740
Analysis complete. Pilot's 
safety can be guaranteed.

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:42.970
It's hard to hold back, isn't it?

00:08:44.270 --> 00:08:45.250
Impact.

00:08:57.660 --> 00:09:01.330
B-Bartfort wins!

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:03.080
Tell me it's not true!

00:09:03.080 --> 00:09:05.390
I refuse to accept the result of this duel!

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:08.900
Try not to gamble too much, everyone.

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:10.460
You can't be serious!

00:09:10.460 --> 00:09:11.450
Coward!

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:12.400
Cheater!

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:15.490
I managed to defeat them.

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:17.410
The prince is merely unconscious.

00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:22.350
I-I see. I appreciate your 
help with this matter.

00:09:22.770 --> 00:09:24.600
Allow me to thank you later.

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:30.700
Mr. Leon, why were you so cruel 
to the prince and his friends?

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:33.170
Everyone's angry with you. Going forward...

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:36.340
I'm the only bad guy they need.

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:34.910
Die!

00:09:34.910 --> 00:09:36.920
Back country baron!

00:09:36.350 --> 00:09:36.920
Huh?

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:38.900
Don't worry about it.

00:09:38.900 --> 00:09:41.430
I'll probably end up leaving 
the academy anyway.

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:42.670
What?

00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:51.270
I'm so glad you're all right, Your Highness.

00:09:51.930 --> 00:09:53.780
How can you be so shameless?

00:09:55.340 --> 00:09:59.870
Everything I've done until 
now has been for you.

00:10:00.140 --> 00:10:02.850
Do you know what my favorite food is?

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:06.050
Yes. As far as soups go, the Seberg region's—

00:10:06.050 --> 00:10:07.370
No.

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:12.150
I liked the grilled skewers 
I had after I snuck out.

00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:16.880
I couldn't say so because I'd be told 
peasant food isn't appropriate for me.

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:19.610
But Marie noticed.

00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:23.890
When we first went out together, 
she took me to a food stall.

00:10:24.370 --> 00:10:25.990
I thought it was fate.

00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:31.060
I know it's rude to both you and your family.

00:10:31.060 --> 00:10:34.900
But Marie is the only one I can love.

00:10:35.140 --> 00:10:39.260
B-But I... I still want to be by your side.

00:10:40.590 --> 00:10:43.530
I can't love you.

00:10:48.550 --> 00:10:49.810
I understand.

00:10:52.090 --> 00:10:55.880
I shall pray for your happiness 
from the sidelines.

00:11:01.350 --> 00:11:04.510
I wish you would've said that sooner.

00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:10.710
I have no connections with the royal palace,

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:15.190
so I thought since you're the 
head of the Redgrave family...

00:11:15.610 --> 00:11:18.940
You want me to clean up your mess?

00:11:19.260 --> 00:11:24.950
I'd like my life to be spared and 
my family not be held responsible.

00:11:26.470 --> 00:11:29.930
You did volunteer to be 
my daughter's champion.

00:11:29.930 --> 00:11:31.710
I'll do the minimum the circumstances demand.

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:34.490
I'll forfeit my title as knight.

00:11:34.490 --> 00:11:38.960
I intend to decline the barony 
I'm being offered, too.

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:40.270
Oh?

00:11:40.270 --> 00:11:43.880
You could've avoided this trouble entirely.

00:11:43.880 --> 00:11:45.470
What do you really want?

00:11:45.860 --> 00:11:49.710
<i>I just wanted to strike a blow 
against those irritating hunks</i>

00:11:49.710 --> 00:11:52.780
<i>and escape this wife-hunting hell.</i>

00:11:53.530 --> 00:11:54.870
I did it for the kingdom.

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:59.230
I couldn't allow the prince to continue 
to be deceived by that woman.

00:12:03.390 --> 00:12:06.060
If that's true, then I'm impressed.

00:12:06.380 --> 00:12:10.090
Angie's engagement to the prince 
has been broken off already.

00:12:10.090 --> 00:12:12.000
My daughter isn't a good match for him.

00:12:12.860 --> 00:12:15.500
By the way, I do have one request.

00:12:16.070 --> 00:12:17.240
What is it?

00:12:17.240 --> 00:12:20.510
This incident has left my daughter 
feeling utterly defeated.

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:26.170
I'd like to give her the chance to rest 
in the countryside for a change of pace.

00:12:29.610 --> 00:12:32.820
<i>All right. This will allow 
me to avoid being executed,</i>

00:12:32.820 --> 00:12:35.460
<i>and to escape the academy and wife-hunting.</i>

00:12:35.960 --> 00:12:37.770
<i>My only regrets are...</i>

00:12:38.120 --> 00:12:40.780
<i>that I couldn't learn 
about tea from my master,</i>

00:12:41.080 --> 00:12:43.030
<i>and Daniel and Raymond.</i>

00:12:43.540 --> 00:12:47.910
<i>I'm disappointed I never got to try all the 
desserts at the academy cafeteria, either.</i>

00:12:50.550 --> 00:12:54.770
<i>Before I even knew it, I was actually 
enjoying life at the academy.</i>

00:12:56.360 --> 00:12:58.130
So he gave up his status,

00:12:58.130 --> 00:13:02.050
his honor, and even a portion of 
his wealth to admonish the prince.

00:13:02.470 --> 00:13:07.810
Yes. He made enemies of everyone and 
volunteered when no one else offered to help.

00:13:07.810 --> 00:13:11.060
He's as a knight should be.

00:13:11.740 --> 00:13:13.980
Outwardly, that is.

00:13:18.110 --> 00:13:19.560
How laughable.

00:13:20.420 --> 00:13:23.690
None of my feelings ever got through to him.

00:13:24.180 --> 00:13:28.200
All I've done is get Leon kicked out of 
the academy because of my selfishness.

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:31.260
Ms. Angelica, you didn't do anything wrong.

00:13:31.850 --> 00:13:33.580
Mr. Leon said he intended

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:38.210
from the start to play the villain 
and leave the academy.

00:13:38.780 --> 00:13:43.460
But I went to see the prince 
without thanking Leon properly.

00:13:44.410 --> 00:13:46.470
I truly am a terrible woman.

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:47.950
Ms. Angelica...

00:13:47.950 --> 00:13:52.220
How sad. Are you not going to talk to them?

00:13:52.780 --> 00:13:56.210
Don't expect me to say anything thoughtful.

00:13:56.550 --> 00:14:00.390
Talking about it won't fix anything, 
so I don't want to get involved.

00:14:00.390 --> 00:14:03.110
You're refreshingly worthless, aren't you?

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:05.990
Yeah, I know I am.

00:14:08.230 --> 00:14:10.370
Dinner is ready.

00:14:10.670 --> 00:14:14.370
The duke's maids are preparing her room.

00:14:14.600 --> 00:14:16.150
That idiot.

00:14:16.150 --> 00:14:21.250
First he picks a fight with the prince, 
and now he's bringing home a duke's daughter.

00:14:21.250 --> 00:14:23.930
Can't he show a little more 
consideration for my poor heart?

00:14:24.730 --> 00:14:27.620
Who are you people? Out of the way.

00:14:27.620 --> 00:14:28.630
Z-Zola...

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:34.140
The royal capital is in an uproar 
because of your incompetent son!

00:14:34.410 --> 00:14:37.050
I-I'm thunderstruck, as well.

00:14:37.050 --> 00:14:39.640
Call that idiot here right—

00:14:40.170 --> 00:14:42.900
Welcome back, my lady.

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:46.900
"My lady"? Just whose daughter are you?

00:14:47.190 --> 00:14:49.150
The Redgrave family's.

00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:50.160
<i>Red...</i>

00:14:50.570 --> 00:14:52.520
You must be Lady Bartfort.

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:56.390
Your son, Lord Leon, has done much for me.

00:14:56.390 --> 00:14:57.160
What?

00:14:57.470 --> 00:15:02.620
I have accepted Lord Leon's kind 
offer to spend my holiday here.

00:15:02.620 --> 00:15:06.520
I-I see. In that case, make yourself at home.

00:15:06.520 --> 00:15:10.060
I must be leaving now, though.

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:16.780
<i>That was so friggin' cool! 
Ms. Angelica is the best!</i>

00:15:16.780 --> 00:15:20.690
Seems like you have a lot to deal with.

00:15:22.410 --> 00:15:25.940
Wow, so this is Mr. Leon's island.

00:15:26.330 --> 00:15:28.190
It's a wonderful island.

00:15:28.690 --> 00:15:30.990
It's still under development.

00:15:30.990 --> 00:15:35.580
It's amazing. I've never 
seen such a beautiful place.

00:15:36.930 --> 00:15:38.080
What's that smell?

00:15:38.350 --> 00:15:40.820
Oh, that's our famous...

00:15:43.220 --> 00:15:46.960
Wow. Ms. Angelica, your hair is beautiful.

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:48.430
It's so glossy.

00:15:48.430 --> 00:15:51.590
The prince said he likes long hair.

00:15:52.190 --> 00:15:54.460
Perhaps I'll try trimming it.

00:15:59.050 --> 00:16:02.670
<i>Perhaps it's because the prince said 
he doesn't like busty women, but...</i>

00:16:06.570 --> 00:16:08.640
I'm jealous of you.

00:16:08.640 --> 00:16:10.740
You and Leon are lovers, are you not?

00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:15.110
O-Oh, no. Our standings are too different.

00:16:15.110 --> 00:16:17.990
Mr. Leon is out of my reach.

00:16:18.380 --> 00:16:21.870
Besides, doesn't Mr. Leon 
have feelings for you?

00:16:22.240 --> 00:16:27.380
What? Impossible. I'm an awful woman.

00:16:28.430 --> 00:16:31.270
We're both dealing with a lot, aren't we?

00:16:31.850 --> 00:16:32.760
Indeed.

00:16:36.500 --> 00:16:38.980
Your skin is so smooth, Olivia.

00:16:38.980 --> 00:16:43.090
But Ms. Angelica, you have 
such smooth hair and skin.

00:16:44.270 --> 00:16:46.310
<i>Why are they so happy?</i>

00:16:49.780 --> 00:16:51.280
What is it, Ms. Olivia?

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:56.670
Um, it's Livia. Please call me Livia.

00:16:57.530 --> 00:16:59.070
Is that all right?

00:16:59.070 --> 00:17:02.540
Everyone back home calls me Livia.

00:17:02.780 --> 00:17:05.310
In that case, call me Angie.

00:17:05.310 --> 00:17:07.840
That's what my friends call me.

00:17:07.840 --> 00:17:08.670
Are you sure?

00:17:08.950 --> 00:17:13.710
Though I doubt you want to be friends 
with such an unpleasant woman.

00:17:13.710 --> 00:17:16.600
Y-You shouldn't talk about yourself that way.

00:17:16.600 --> 00:17:20.180
Ms. Angelica, you—Angie, 
you're a wonderful woman.

00:17:20.400 --> 00:17:22.510
I'm the worst.

00:17:22.510 --> 00:17:25.180
I still resent Marie more than I can bear.

00:17:25.720 --> 00:17:29.190
I've thought numerous times 
about getting revenge.

00:17:29.630 --> 00:17:32.030
I don't think there's 
anything wrong with that.

00:17:32.030 --> 00:17:34.440
You want revenge? Fine by me.

00:17:34.910 --> 00:17:36.450
Let's do it.

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:40.450
It's all right for me to seek revenge?

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:44.430
Mr. Leon, don't encourage Angie.

00:17:44.430 --> 00:17:47.460
I know the best way to get revenge.

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:49.250
R-Really?

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:51.340
Angie, don't take the bait!

00:17:52.150 --> 00:17:57.470
The best way to get revenge 
is to become happy yourself.

00:17:59.940 --> 00:18:03.380
Trying to make someone else 
unhappy is a waste of time.

00:18:03.380 --> 00:18:07.170
Spending your time on yourself 
is far more meaningful.

00:18:07.170 --> 00:18:08.820
Y-You're right.

00:18:09.160 --> 00:18:11.610
In that case, I'll support you.

00:18:12.030 --> 00:18:15.490
Angie, let us devote ourselves 
to revenge together.

00:18:17.140 --> 00:18:20.320
<i>The protagonist and the 
rival make a powerful team.</i>

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:24.990
<i>I almost feel sorry for Marie that 
these two are working against her.</i>

00:18:24.990 --> 00:18:27.000
Wh-What do you mean?

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:32.380
You're all being disinherited 
and losing your statuses?

00:18:32.710 --> 00:18:36.630
It's exactly what it sounds like. 
I'm no longer the crown prince.

00:18:38.380 --> 00:18:41.420
Now I can have a proper 
relationship with you.

00:18:41.420 --> 00:18:43.400
We've made up our minds.

00:18:43.830 --> 00:18:48.390
This is the decision we've made. 
Sorry to have kept you waiting, Marie.

00:18:48.120 --> 00:18:50.650
Marie... Marie... Marie... Marie...

00:18:49.220 --> 00:18:49.890
<i>Are...</i>

00:18:50.200 --> 00:18:52.020
<i>Are they stupid?!</i>

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:54.910
<i>Now they're just unemployed rich kids!</i>

00:18:55.240 --> 00:19:01.280
I can no longer formally stand by your side, 
but I'll be wishing for your happiness.

00:19:03.020 --> 00:19:06.200
We'll protect Marie for you, Julius.

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:08.920
We need to get revenge on Leon, too.

00:19:08.920 --> 00:19:10.970
It'd be no fun leaving things as they are.

00:19:10.970 --> 00:19:14.300
Perhaps we should start adventuring 
and search for Lost Items.

00:19:14.300 --> 00:19:17.550
I feel relieved knowing you'll 
all be protecting Marie.

00:19:18.580 --> 00:19:20.650
<i>You can't be serious!</i>

00:19:20.650 --> 00:19:24.900
<i>Gorgeous dresses, luxurious meals, and 
the life at the royal palace I dreamed of...</i>

00:19:24.900 --> 00:19:27.060
<i>All of that is...</i>

00:19:27.410 --> 00:19:30.560
Why is this happening?!

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:31.640
Marie...

00:19:31.640 --> 00:19:34.060
I can't believe you're crying tears of joy.

00:19:34.780 --> 00:19:37.320
Between the broken off engagements, the duel,

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:41.150
and the prince's disinheritance, there's 
been quite an uproar at the royal palace.

00:19:41.150 --> 00:19:42.460
I see.

00:19:42.460 --> 00:19:45.070
What will happen to our family?

00:19:45.420 --> 00:19:50.080
Don't worry. Neither Lord Leon nor 
your family will be held responsible.

00:19:50.470 --> 00:19:52.830
R-Really?

00:19:53.330 --> 00:19:55.890
<i>Good thing I talked to Angie's dad.</i>

00:19:55.890 --> 00:20:00.380
Instead, Lord Leon will 
be granted a formal title.

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:00.840
<i>Huh?</i>

00:20:01.110 --> 00:20:04.650
After all, you're the knight who admonished 
the prince's foolish behavior.

00:20:04.650 --> 00:20:05.350
What?

00:20:06.390 --> 00:20:09.850
Your royal ranking has been increased 
to upper sixth rank. Congratulations.

00:20:09.850 --> 00:20:14.850
<i>Nobody said I'd be promoted!</i>

00:20:17.790 --> 00:20:20.550
<i>Apparently even being made 
a knight at 16 years old</i>

00:20:20.550 --> 00:20:22.860
<i>is unprecedented in the Holfort Kingdom.</i>

00:20:23.940 --> 00:20:26.870
<i>It was Julius's parents 
who granted me the title.</i>

00:20:28.130 --> 00:20:30.120
<i>I'm sure they must've 
had complicated feelings</i>

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:32.370
<i>toward the guy who beat up their own son.</i>

00:20:32.940 --> 00:20:35.060
<i>And receiving the royal palace's recognition</i>

00:20:35.060 --> 00:20:37.880
<i>meant I wouldn't be leaving 
the academy anymore.</i>

00:20:38.790 --> 00:20:40.380
What's he doing here?

00:20:40.380 --> 00:20:42.690
Didn't he leave the academy?

00:20:42.690 --> 00:20:44.410
This sucks.

00:20:45.250 --> 00:20:48.140
Finding a wife will be even harder now.

00:20:48.140 --> 00:20:54.170
Regarding Marie and Julius and his friends, 
apparently they've stayed together.

00:20:54.170 --> 00:20:56.150
Yeah, I figured.

00:20:56.590 --> 00:21:02.150
Though they're no longer lovers, 
they've taken on several dungeons together.

00:21:02.730 --> 00:21:05.590
They're training to defeat you.

00:21:05.590 --> 00:21:07.630
Since they've lost the 
backing of their families,

00:21:07.630 --> 00:21:10.120
they've needed to earn their own funds.

00:21:10.120 --> 00:21:11.910
They all seemed to be enjoying themselves,

00:21:12.710 --> 00:21:14.540
with the exception of Marie.

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:16.980
That's unusually good news from you.

00:21:16.980 --> 00:21:19.400
I'll be able sleep soundly tonight.

00:21:20.230 --> 00:21:23.530
Mr. Leon, there you are.

00:21:23.530 --> 00:21:25.300
Are you alone again today?

00:21:25.300 --> 00:21:29.760
Yeah, alone again today. 
Thanks for ripping my heart out.

00:21:29.760 --> 00:21:33.660
Can't you do something about 
that foul language of yours?

00:21:33.660 --> 00:21:35.060
If you're not busy, come with us.

00:21:35.550 --> 00:21:38.440
We've found a crêperie 
that's supposed to be good.

00:21:38.440 --> 00:21:39.700
Come on, let's go.

00:21:40.290 --> 00:21:41.570
Hurry.

00:21:41.990 --> 00:21:45.450
<i>I can't believe I've got these two 
cute, kind girls right next to me,</i>

00:21:45.450 --> 00:21:47.700
<i>and I can't do anything with either of them.</i>

00:21:49.380 --> 00:21:53.330
<i>The world of otome games 
is truly tough for mobs.</i>

00:21:55.040 --> 00:21:57.710
<b>Trapped in a Dating Sim</b>

00:23:25.510 --> 00:23:27.960
Mr. Leon, what do you think? 
Does this look good on me?

00:23:27.960 --> 00:23:29.260
Yeah, you look super cute!

00:23:29.260 --> 00:23:31.260
I haven't worn this in a while. 
What do you think?

00:23:31.260 --> 00:23:32.560
You look dignified and cool!

00:23:32.560 --> 00:23:35.230
How do I look? Does this look good on me?

00:23:35.230 --> 00:23:35.970
Buzz off, dude.

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:36.660
Next time.

00:23:36.660 --> 00:23:37.710
A cultural festival?

00:23:37.710 --> 00:23:38.620
It'll be my first.

00:23:38.620 --> 00:23:40.350
What? Am I the only odd one out?
